{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":52.38999938964844,"text":"This temple holds a record nobody ever envied. It took about 638 years to finish. Work started in the 6th century BC and stopped when the city changed rulers. It stood half-built for so long that ancient writers used it as an example of overambition. It was finally completed by the Roman emperor Hadrian in AD 131, who put two enormous statues inside, one of Zeus and one of himself. It had 104 columns, each about 17 meters tall. Fifteen are standing today. There is a sixteenth on the ground. A storm blew it over in 1852 and nobody ever picked it up. It is the best thing there to look at, because it fell like a tower of bricks and its pieces rolled out in a line, like a sliced loaf. That is how you learn a column was never one single stone.","words":[{"word":"This","start":0,"end":0.6399999856948853},{"word":"temple","start":0.6399999856948853,"end":0.9800000190734863},{"word":"holds","start":0.9800000190734863,"end":1.2799999713897705},{"word":"a","start":1.2799999713897705,"end":1.8600000143051147},{"word":"record","start":1.8600000143051147,"end":1.8600000143051147},{"word":"nobody","start":1.8600000143051147,"end":2.380000114440918},{"word":"ever","start":2.380000114440918,"end":2.819999933242798},{"word":"envied","start":2.819999933242798,"end":3.0999999046325684},{"word":"It","start":3.700000047683716,"end":3.700000047683716},{"word":"took","start":3.700000047683716,"end":3.859999895095825},{"word":"about","start":3.859999895095825,"end":4.199999809265137},{"word":"638","start":4.199999809265137,"end":5.539999961853027},{"word":"years","start":5.539999961853027,"end":6},{"word":"to","start":6,"end":6.320000171661377},{"word":"finish","start":6.320000171661377,"end":6.599999904632568},{"word":"Work","start":7.460000038146973,"end":7.460000038146973},{"word":"started","start":7.460000038146973,"end":7.800000190734863},{"word":"in","start":7.800000190734863,"end":7.960000038146973},{"wor